  "forceSea": {
    "notes": "Sheet px polygons of water (sea, or lake when enclosed by land) hidden under decorations or misread as land: the inner end of Blackwater Bay under the Targaryen crest and a small house crest beside King's Landing (the city stands on the bay at the river mouth: kings-landing-river-mouth); island and castle names lettered on the sea with cream halos that the trace took for land (map critic, 2026-10-08): 'Dragonstone', 'Dragonstone Castle', 'Driftmark', the Velaryon shield; the Eastwatch-by-the-Sea labels on the Bay of Seals; 'Lordsport' and 'Pyke' off Pyke; the 'Isle of Faces' lettering filling the Gods Eye's north third (the island itself is the small one under the marker); the 'Storm's End' lettering on Shipbreaker Bay below the castle marker (it made a 49 km false peninsula), the diagonal 'Shipbreaker Bay' label and the sea half of 'Evenfall Hall' off Tarth; the Trident's mouth, whose estuary the Maidenpool crest cuts off from the Bay of Crabs (trident-course, trident-mouth): without it the estuary reads as a lake the river trace never reaches and the riverlands' rivers have no outlet; at Sunspear, the inlet between the castle's spit and the mainland (traced as river ink inside land) and the 'Sunspear' and 'Water Gardens' labels lettered on the sea.",
